---
description: Group related buttons together with consistent spacing and alignment.
---

<script>
  import { Button, ButtonSet } from "carbon-components-svelte";
  import Login from "carbon-icons-svelte/lib/Login.svelte";
</script>

For a custom modal or panel footer that needs size-aware stacking (one to four actions, ordered automatically by `kind`), use [ActionSet](/components/ActionSet) instead, which wraps `ButtonSet` with that behavior built in. [Modal](/components/Modal) builds its footer from props.

## Basic

Place buttons side by side in a horizontal layout.

<ButtonSet>
  <Button kind="secondary">Cancel</Button>
  <Button>Submit</Button>
</ButtonSet>

## Stacked

Set `stacked` to `true` to stack the buttons vertically instead of side by side.

<ButtonSet stacked>
  <Button icon={Login}>Log in</Button>
  <Button kind="ghost">Sign up</Button>
</ButtonSet>

## Responsive stacked

Set `stacked` to a breakpoint object to stack the buttons on narrow viewports and lay them out side by side from a given breakpoint up, instead of reading `window.innerWidth` in your own code. Keys map to Carbon's breakpoints (`sm`, `md`, `lg`, `xlg`, `max`) and resolve mobile-first. Resize the browser to see the buttons below unstack at `md`.

<ButtonSet stacked={{ sm: true, md: false }}>
  <Button kind="secondary">Cancel</Button>
  <Button>Submit</Button>
</ButtonSet>